--
N5008 [expr.unary.op]/4: the address of a member forms a pointer to member
only for a qualified-id `&C::m'; [expr.prim.id.general]/4: in a default
member initializer an unqualified member name `x' is transformed into
`(*this).x', so `&x' has type `int *'. The front end typed the NSDMI `int
*p = &x;' as a pointer to member ("invalid implicit conversion from
'signed int (struct s:: *)' to 'signed int *'") and rejected the unit: the
initializer of a class without a user-provided constructor was type-
checked in class scope without `this'; the same initializer in a
constructor's mem-initializer works. Found while testing
cpp11_parenthesized_member_dereference_in_member_function. g++ 13 and
clang++ 18 accept the program. Fails on bin53.
